<title>NETHERLANDS: KLM shares rise on H1 profit rise.</title>
<headline>KLM shares rise on H1 profit rise.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in flag carrier KLM Royal Dutch Airlines were up 2.50 guilders at 44.40 on Tuesday after the company reported first half net profits of 529 million guilders, up from 437 million a year earlier.</p>
<p>The result was in the middle of a wide band of analysts' forecasts, which ranged from 457 to 639 million guilders for the half year to September 30.</p>
<p>KLM also said it expected to see improved operating income, except for fuel costs, year-on-year in the second half.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
